  "body": "A deburr now leaves each edge run straight up to the clearance plane before it travels to the next. It used to rapid diagonally from cutting depth, with the cone still in the break, up and across the part.\n\n### What was wrong\n\n- `finishing3d::deburr` opened every run with `Rapid` to `(next start, clearance)` from wherever the previous run ended: the tip `drop` below the edge, the cone touching the break it just cut. Only the last run got a vertical retract.\n- On `main` 8f30bee, the brick from `operations.rs`'s deburr test (stock = the brick, `CM-0600-90`, width 2, window z 6..8) gives `Rapid (20,-10,8) -> (-20,10,25)`. Verify convicts `RapidInStock` at moves 3, 8 and 13, so the post is blocked.\n\n### What changed\n\n- `deburr::retract`: a vertical rapid from where the path stands to the clearance plane, or nothing when it's already there. It runs before every run's traverse and once at the end, replacing the old inline final retract, so the path's end is unchanged.\n- Cut moves don't change. The existing deburr tests compare cut points and pass as before. No golden holds a deburr path.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/304-deburr-retract.md` (a feed retract, and a retract plane, were considered and dropped).\n\n### Tests\n\n- `crates/motion/tests/deburr.rs`: `every_run_leaves_its_cut_straight_up_before_the_next_traverse`. A closed box rides as several runs, and every rapid that starts below clearance is vertical and ends at clearance.\n- New `crates/app/tests/deburr_links.rs`: `a_deburr_on_a_finished_brick_links_its_runs_without_a_rapid_in_stock`. Through the commands, on a finished part: no `RapidInStock`, and no diagonal rapid from cutting depth.\n- With `deburr.rs` put back to `main` (`git stash` of that file only), both fail: \"rapid 10 leaves cutting depth diagonally: (40, 0, -12) -> (0, 20, 20)\", and \"a link rapids through the part: [RapidInStock { at: 3 }, RapidInStock { at: 8 }, RapidInStock { at: 13 }]\".\n\n### What ran (Windows 10, local, built from upstream `main` 8f30bee plus this commit)\n\n- The quick gate's plan for this diff (`scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick -DryRun`, run by hand with `-j 4`): motion lib plus `deburr` (157 tests), app `deburr_links`. All pass.\n- Every app suite that creates a Deburr operation, too: `operations`, `area_controls`, `project_roundtrip`, `ribbon`, `tool_law`, `probe_op`. With `deburr_links`, 225 pass and 6 ignored (ignored on `main` too).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Not run: the windowed app, Linux, macOS.\n- Not fixed here: the deburr's intended break still reads as a gouge to the post gate (#303), so a deburr still can't post until that's decided. This PR removes the part of the refusal that was a real motion fault.\n\nChangelog: A deburr leaves each edge run straight up to the clearance plane instead of rapiding diagonally from cutting depth through the part (#304)\n\nFixes #304\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
